License: GPL-3+

Files: ohscore/dsp/nr.py ohscore/dsp/nr_tables.npz
Copyright: 2015, 2025, 2026 Warren Pratt, NR0V <warren@wpratt.com>
           2026 Brian Henderson <noreply@openhamshack.com>
License: GPL-2+
Comment: The receive noise reduction is a numpy port of emnr.c from WDSP
 2.10 (https://github.com/TAPR/OpenHPSDR-wdsp, b02d5bac), and
 nr_tables.npz holds WDSP's GG and GGS gain tables from its calculus.c.
 WDSP is under GPL version 2 or later; this port is distributed under
 version 3 or later, as the rest of the program.

Files: ohscore/ohsdigi.abi3.so
Copyright: 2026 Brian Henderson <noreply@openhamshack.com>
           2001-2023 Joe Taylor K1JT, Steve Franke K9AN, Bill Somerville G4WJS,
           Nico Palermo IV3NWV and the WSJT Development Group
           2023-present PyO3 Project and Contributors
           The Rust Project Developers (libc, the Rust standard library)
           Aleksey Kladov (once_cell)
           Kurt Moraw DJ0ABR (HSmodem)
           2007-2020 Joseph Gaeddert (liquid-dsp)
License: GPL-3+ and MIT
Comment: ohsdigi, the FT8/FT4 encoder in the amd64 and arm64 packages, is
 built from rust/ohsdigi in OpenHamShack's own source (GPL-3+; published at
 the address in the Source field above), much of it
 ported from WSJT-X 2.7.0 (https://wsjt.sourceforge.io/, GPL-3+). Compiled
 into it are PyO3 0.29.3, pyo3-ffi, libc 0.2.190, once_cell 1.21.4 and the
 Rust 1.98.1 standard library, each offered under MIT or Apache-2.0 and
 used here under MIT (rust/ohsdigi/LICENSE-THIRD-PARTY lists them). Its
 HSmodem module (the QO-100 multimedia beacon's modem) is ported from
 HSmodem (https://github.com/amsat-dl/QO-100-Modem, GPL-2+) and from
 liquid-dsp (https://github.com/jgaeddert/liquid-dsp, MIT).

